.TH env_set 3
.SH NAME
env_set \- set an environment variable
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <env.h>

.B int env_set(const char* \fIname\fP, const char* \fIvalue\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B env_set
sets the environment variable \fIname\fP to \fIvalue\fP. On Windows, 
it uses the native Win32 API. On POSIX systems, it wraps the environment 
update functions.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 on failure.